From: Pixelado Dev <350114043+pixeladodev@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Room pause: the menu always pauses, in a local wireless session the whole room

The in-game menu used to keep a local wireless game running behind it (kms.menu_live, mh_live),
with its sound lowered and stuttering even for a host alone. Now it always pauses the game, and in a
session it pauses everyone: Emu::room_hold_set tells the room (melonDS LAN's Cmd_Hold, through the
host), and each console's emulator thread stops at a frame's end while another player holds it,
servicing the network every 10 ms meanwhile so all of them start again within a few ms. Emu::
net_resumed resets the MP waits' wall-clock counts after a pause.

A console paused by someone else's menu can show it (bmenu_wait: who is in the menu, that the game
goes on when they leave it); Pixelado Party draws that screen when it runs the engine (0008), and
menu.c's bmenu_wait is a stub, so without Party the frontend waits without a screen of its own.
START (or L3) opens the console's own menu over the same pause. Two players opening theirs at once
hold it together; a player that leaves the session (or a host that goes) lets go of it. menu.h:
room_hold, bmenu_wait, the players' hold. The quit, the room page and the pop-ups are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---

